          "title": "Current Members — Neil M. Gorsuch",
          "published_at": null,
          "checked_at": "2026-10-18",
          "excerpt": "Neil M. Gorsuch, Associate Justice, was born in Denver, Colorado, August 29, 1967. He received a B.A. from Columbia University, a J.D. from Harvard Law School, and a D.Phil. from Oxford University. He took his seat on April 10, 2017.",
          "tier": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "s2",
          "url": "https://www.fjc.gov/history/judges/gorsuch-neil-m",
          "title": "Gorsuch, Neil M. | Federal Judicial Center",
          "published_at": null,
          "checked_at": "2026-10-18",
          "excerpt": "Columbia University, B.A., 1988; Harvard Law School, J.D., 1991; University of Oxford, D.Phil., 2004. Law clerk, Hon. David B. Sentelle, U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit, 1991-1992; Law clerk, Hon. Byron R. White and Anthony M. Kennedy, Supreme Court of the United States, 1993-1994; Private practice, Washington, D.C., 1995-2005; Principal deputy to the associate attorney general and acting associate attorney general, U.S. Department of Justice, 2005-2006. Commission issued on August 8, 2006. Service terminated on April 9, 2017.",
          "tier": 1
        },
